#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073495 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ffe13c6-a2b6-5d70-8ebe-d152ae4db35f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Multiplication Problem Corresponding to a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "f26ed088-6f0b-56b8-9027-9b9af4bcf415" :question/math-academy-id "e-14484" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4f5bfdd38a8c02510e86279ac548a2a6b889f9eb33a8ef8c273fd2e384e54b72.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/b4/b43d5a0e0a44e6d418a901dc9fa806079b1b9425fc111640439e4338f8bf0d84.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073498 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f3ddce4-2cf8-5bf6-86d3-8c304ee6c241" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Missing Number in a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "a653f45f-e638-5646-a55c-13b319e511b0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14490" :question/problem "What number is missing from the multiplication problem below?\n\n![](images/69/69f859c61c693f7ece01fef8f829fdc772acae77e90be97b7b093fb9849acc95.png)" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/dc/dcb89325ddd68043c9edf2f595a7a7d89b3ba078bbb1805af7bea58867f627b6.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts by horizontal lines. So, the shaded part on the left is $\\color{blue}3$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}{3}} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073499 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd1c12d-acb6-5961-a248-47f172fe5bef" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Model Corresponding to a Multiplication Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "9bc02e5b-5028-5aa1-85d8-c1217b425c36" :question/math-academy-id "e-14491" :question/problem "What picture is missing from the multiplication model below?\n\n![](images/39/39c8668bd4bf5309b708769a99d9d3fa2184f0937411d437de8a1195853e5118.png)" :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we are multiplying by $\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}$, we need to split the whole into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/65/6584c694fbbc990dfa3b58a19545d3deb9889f162da6e02a9820310a190ae04e.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nThe missing picture is:\n\n![](images/e3/e349233ebb5e3927f0d4bda98cb2470c1f17574a522d2f4b9cbddaf365fe946d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073500 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e2265e-5c75-538f-91a1-9120d2f77c9e" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Fraction by a Unit Fraction Using a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "4730b433-9614-58ea-a452-e404c237ba3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14492" :question/problem "![](images/82/82439d51448a442dede4b3965ecbbd2f2daa7b2365ea75c80951478fd10af65c.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\dfrac{4}{5} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to multiply by $\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}3}$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/a9/a95b378064e6ec2ed15637fd05ea49e5f988bfb30d8ae788a7b2086ff920a65f.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{4}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{5} \\times \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac{4}{15}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ffe13c6-a2b6-5d70-8ebe-d152ae4db35f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Multiplication Problem Corresponding to a Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "156eeca8-010b-5a5d-8f2e-9ae2f2d453e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425790} {:answer/id #uuid "5946b4d9-3393-52bf-af46-3294c0d1d64b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425796} {:answer/id #uuid "5feb693e-76f6-53e8-a3f3-ae995f431925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425797} {:answer/id #uuid "b3cc370e-b400-5538-8454-bd77916d61a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425804} {:answer/id #uuid "e29bf940-a6f1-51a4-83eb-80b4de569488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5feb693e-76f6-53e8-a3f3-ae995f431925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425797} :answer-field/id #uuid "87fea5e6-a276-5797-a7b0-4db1b53ca5a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "952e22b6-fb4f-5a48-8331-618041da94da" :question/math-academy-id "q-137179" :question/problem "![](images/26/26520b2b179e8d2bac0b20552d670d8503d734d22bafacb741edb2efce649f4d.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{2}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{10}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/40/40183e8f591be9be4dbffc83e45958d184674a4bb83dc83df5a4149cf70b8468.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073684 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ffe13c6-a2b6-5d70-8ebe-d152ae4db35f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Multiplication Problem Corresponding to a Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50394559-8014-56f5-a0d3-b473b0728be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425793} {:answer/id #uuid "a3be83f1-a912-526f-9676-53a37328709b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425802} {:answer/id #uuid "d50b8042-9450-53fc-b01c-9d37b4604c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425812} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ab4e25-3e39-5b51-98e1-2f788fbb1292" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425815} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f51e1e-bfbb-5304-b9d4-16a5cf0b1ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9f51e1e-bfbb-5304-b9d4-16a5cf0b1ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425819} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eccb805-31a2-5b51-9c68-a40284d36e95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88cf76f9-070e-56c7-8184-71a9b98899fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-137180" :question/problem "![](images/b7/b7e7ec3356ed3e6eb90075bf8e148b0d3836be7df7551ccac31ffffcb9800ea8.png)\n\nWhat multiplication problem is represented by the model above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\frac{3}{8}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/50/5091a3f982e94ea27aea26a45b47bf768980dbc802f52905d0ecfc78e111f3ef.png)\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{8}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f3ddce4-2cf8-5bf6-86d3-8c304ee6c241" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Missing Number in a Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a7310b-913f-55c7-b182-39be76669a94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425791} {:answer/id #uuid "55309ed7-4c44-5ddb-8208-db7b76f9384b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425795} {:answer/id #uuid "60fb4716-8b36-5682-9810-2a38551a2744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425798} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a31fbd-5b49-5328-a37e-224c355fff82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425810} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f44dd0-6611-5eea-bf7f-a9815cc649f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7f44dd0-6611-5eea-bf7f-a9815cc649f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425816} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a5dba11-a208-5184-ace8-45204831aa81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f128125-7113-569b-86a4-d5760981b530" :question/math-academy-id "q-137402" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c66fe5af6ee7cb43a1327b530027971c60f4b656cd837b305cacafc9cd04307d.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the multiplication problem above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{2}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{10}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/84/849573cc74dfd2c51479ae3c9c13e8993cfa7cf433887198abda16fe34704eb7.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $2$ equal parts by a horizontal line. So, the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd1c12d-acb6-5961-a248-47f172fe5bef" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Model Corresponding to a Multiplication Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "986f6a73-fa3d-54f4-aa01-6a9add3ce52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/15/15b0e5a56d012b3a0e6556e11c5da14a5ff3f13746d9dec57444f8d0521d298b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425799} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e4cef7-53a4-5d10-a58f-8d4b2743049a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b1/b1e7f6acf290441552d18d46141438b98eaf954d4522fa934d0eaaac4dcb94b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425807} {:answer/id #uuid "babf0d93-a722-5dec-9a3e-34a9b115512a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a483cf94baee1222f043c2807b23b0249281b8a22f190a6cc311312c677ac07.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425808} {:answer/id #uuid "d042aeda-4b19-5c10-8ef7-a052c8698ed2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f1/f1f7ecca69164ce74359bf8e7b4efd3c29d48b47248710561042d0551a4a266d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425811} {:answer/id #uuid "f91ac2a3-d1f3-591b-8e45-3bd4427f5253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3b528fa9a0ff896ca9acda66f1bb2472550e871d044f08a44f1fcfe7a0319ad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "babf0d93-a722-5dec-9a3e-34a9b115512a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a483cf94baee1222f043c2807b23b0249281b8a22f190a6cc311312c677ac07.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425808} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a198355-1ace-51d6-add6-fa89a4dc5132" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c07fb2aa-7b2a-5715-9eb3-94df22bf1924" :question/math-academy-id "q-137425" :question/problem "![](images/31/3167905fdd4699c03f0db5f70f21dc7512a4d24bec7918f3b040259e5c618f5b.png)\n\nWhat picture is missing from the multiplication model above?" :question/worked-solution "In the model, we have $\\frac{1}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/02/0205f15c05454f0d98ae4bbc4c0c8598cbcff880115390a5887a277ceb3f1c4a.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{1}{12}$ of the whole.\n\nThe missing picture is:\n\n![](images/6a/6a483cf94baee1222f043c2807b23b0249281b8a22f190a6cc311312c677ac07.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f3ddce4-2cf8-5bf6-86d3-8c304ee6c241" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Missing Number in a Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6c98757-3c97-5200-a7f2-0a0514d46039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6c98757-3c97-5200-a7f2-0a0514d46039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425803} :answer-field/id #uuid "07ce1a07-8871-5911-9c9b-077bc1a1b66c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2247508-110b-59bf-98ca-b9f8903d0d7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-210510" :question/problem "Insert the missing number in the multiplication problem below.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" height=\"100\" rules=\"all\" width=\"100\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"3\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$\\times $</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$=$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" height=\"100\" rules=\"all\" width=\"100\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{4}{6}$ on the left and $\\frac{4}{24}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/54/54e0c1ae73fdf546507c8a4f486f911f1ef8f6bfb57da249a1654393a63151b4.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $4$ equal parts by horizontal lines. So, the shaded part on the left is $4$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}\\times \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{4}{24}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073686 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd1c12d-acb6-5961-a248-47f172fe5bef" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Model Corresponding to a Multiplication Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2acdce46-ae09-52a8-87ff-bf7550db9ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/503598e9174ef0276190165b397e5e9d69972e0df9ac6e83a9e4f9258b98fb60.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425792} {:answer/id #uuid "520ed5d8-6c46-5467-ac97-6eaeca88d2f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f1/f160dffa224f97f932636137b2559ebee650ff6be0853206b3b0a89ed2bfab98.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425794} {:answer/id #uuid "9a316a3f-0f60-5ef4-ad90-da870f667e2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186